                         916 --460:  * Function name:  R_FDL_IFct_ChkAccessRight
                         917 --461:  *********************************************************************************************************************/
                         918 --462: /**
                         919 --463:  * The check is a robustness feature against modification from outside the library as the parameter
                         920 --464:  * check during command initiation should have detected any parameter error already. This check
                         921 --465:  * shall block wrong settings directly before starting the Flash hardware. So,
                         922 --466:  * on violation, the returned error is a protection error, not a parameter error. \n
                         923 --467:  * The function reads back the access parameters from the FCU for the check and compares them
                         924 --468:  * against the access rights defined by the descriptor.
                         925 --469:  *
                         926 --470:  * @param[in]  accType_enu - type of FDL access (user or EEL)
                         927 --471:  * @param[in]  granularity_u32 - Granularity for each command, used to determine if start address is aligned properly
                         928 --472:  *
                         929 --473:  * @return     Returns the access check result
                         930 --474:  *             - R_FDL_BUSY (check was OK)
                         931 --475:  *             - R_FDL_ERR_INTERNAL (parameter detected)
                         932 --476:  */
                         933 --477: /*********************************************************************************************************************/
