                        1080 --529:  * @param[in]     to: timeout value (r8)
                        1081 --530:  * @param[out]    ret: timeout check result (r9)
                        1082 --531:  *                     0: No error, 1: Timeout error
                        1083 --532:  * @return        ---
                        1084 --533:  */
                        1085 --534: /*********************************************************************************************************************/
                        1086 --536: /*********************************************************************************************************************
                        1087 --537:  * MISRA Rule:   MISRA-C 2004 rule 3.1 (QAC message 3006)
                        1088 --538:  * Reason:       This function contains a mixture of in-line assembler statements and C statements.
                        1089 --539:  *               The function is copied to RAM into a memory range of fix size. So, the function itself must have a
                        1090 --540:  *               fix size which cannot be realized by a c-compiler. So, the function is written in Assembler
                        1091 --541:  * Verification: Review of the c-interface (only temporary registers are used and the stack size is unchanged
                        1092 --542:  *********************************************************************************************************************/
                        1093 --543: /*********************************************************************************************************************
                        1094 --544:  * MISRA Rule:   MISRA-C 2004 rule 3.1 (QAC message 1006)
                        1095 --545:  * Reason:       In-line assembler construct is a language extension. The code has been ignored.
                        1096 --546:  * Verification: -
                        1097 --547:  *********************************************************************************************************************/
                        1098 --548: /*********************************************************************************************************************
                        1099 --549:  * MISRA Rule:   MISRA-C 2004 rule 3.1 (QAC message 3206)
                        1100 --550:  * Reason:       function parameter seems to be not used in the function as no c-code relates on
                        1101 --551:  *               it, but the assembler code uses the parameter
                        1102 --552:  * Verification: -
                        1103 --553:  *********************************************************************************************************************/
                        1104 --554:  /*********************************************************************************************************************
                        1105 --555:  * MISRA Rule:   MISRA-C 2004 rule 8.10 (QAC message 1505)
                        1106 --556:  * Reason:       Function declared as external usable function, but is only used locally
                        1107 --557:  * Verification: Function must be declared global in order to avoid function inlining. The function contains assembler 
                        1108 --558:  *               code and relies on calling conventions. GHS may (in case of precompiled library creation) optimize by
                        1109 --559:  *               inlining. As the parameters are used in assbembler only, GHS will optimize call parameter preparation 
                        1110 --560:  *               away.
                        1111 --561:  *********************************************************************************************************************/ 
