                        3291 --1881: /**
                        3292 --1882:  * Execute a function in RAM. \n
                        3293 --1883:  * This function copies a function to the RAM and jumps to the RAM.
                        3294 --1884:  * Stack is used as storage location for the function to be copied.
                        3295 --1885:  *
                        3296 --1886:  * @param[in]  pFct         - function to execute
                        3297 --1887:  * @param[in]  param_pu32   - parameter structure that will be used by the function in RAM. The
                        3298 --1888:  *                            structure pointer is just passed to the function.
                        3299 --1889:  * @return     ---
                        3300 --1890:  */
                        3301 --1891: /*********************************************************************************************************************/
                        3302 --1893: /*********************************************************************************************************************
                        3303 --1894:  * MISRA Rule:   MISRA-C 2004 rule 3.1 (QAC message 0310)
                        3304 --1895:  * Reason:       Casting to different object pointer type is used because function code need
                        3305 --1896:  *               to be copied to RAM.
                        3306 --1897:  * Verification: Copy destination is g_fdl_str.
                        3307 --1898:  *              - This is re-initialized afterwards in R_FDL_Init
                        3308 --1899:  *              - Copy size is limited by "sizeof"
                        3309 --1900:  *********************************************************************************************************************/
                        3310 --1902: /*********************************************************************************************************************
                        3311 --1903:  * MISRA Rule:   MISRA-C 2004 rule 11.3 (QAC message 0303, 0305, 0306)
                        3312 --1904:  * Reason:       Casts between a pointer and other data types are used because function
                        3313 --1905:  *               code need to be copied to RAM and finally a jump to RAM is done
                        3314 --1906:  * Verification: None as complete system would crash if this does not work.
                        3315 --1907:  *********************************************************************************************************************/
                        3316 --1909: /********************************************************************************************************************
                        3317 --1910: * MISRA Rule:   MISRA-C 2004 rule 3.1 (QAC message 0491)
                        3318 --1911: * Reason:       Array subscripting applied to an object of pointer type required to copy data to
                        3319 --1912: *               RAM location
                        3320 --1913: * Verification: Check copy boundaries and address
                        3321 --1914: *********************************************************************************************************************/
